Z||000000||Kwez||06-17-2001||03:29 AM||||hehe,<BR>some of you might have seen this one coming after reading my previous post (88 vs 86-87)<P>I'm throwing this one out again : <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20010418-2-005687.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20010418-2-005687.html</A> <P>From Archie's experience w. all the V8 swaps I would think that the trans CAN handle it. I was just wondering since some people say "the Getrag is designed to handle up to 2xxHP but forget about the other ones ..."<P>I understand that the trans is designed for a safe / <B>100% reliable</B> max. amount of torque/HP ... how wide is the margin.<P>anybody w. stick shift trans failure after an engine swap ? (details please)<BR>actual real 1st hand experience  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>vs.<P>still running: how long, how hard, what HP/torque etc. w. a Fiero 5speed ?<P><BR>Thank you for your help||||reg||1
Z||000001||LarryB||06-17-2001||05:25 AM||||There's no such thing as <B>100%</B> reliable.  Any time you're abusive you run a risk of trouble.<P>If you search the forum you'll find a thread from a few months back of a 350 conversion that trashed a Muncie after a couple of hours of <B>admitted abuse</B>. <P>||||reg||1
